course: dictionary
lesson: 5804
title: Magenta, a colour and an ink
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a new word. They often give you clues. «Printers use cyan, magenta and yellow instead, which mix cleaner colours.» Printers mix colours, so magenta must be a colour.
explain: The sentence about the magazine helps too: «magenta (a pinky purple)». Magenta is a bright purplish-red or pinkish-purple colour, and the author gives you a clue with the words in brackets.
explain: Magenta also has a second job in printing. Printers use four inks, cyan, magenta, yellow and black. Look at a picture through a magnifying glass and you will see tiny dots of these inks.
fact: Magenta is a bright purplish-red or pinkish-purple colour.
fact: Magenta is one of the four main printer inks: cyan, magenta, yellow and black (CMYK).
fact: In light, red and blue light together make magenta.
fact: Magenta is named after the town of Magenta in Italy, where a battle took place in 1859.
fact: The magenta dye was discovered in 1859, the same year as that battle.
exercise: «Printers use cyan, magenta and yellow instead, which mix cleaner colours.» What is magenta here? | A type of printer | *A colour | A kind of paper | A town in Italy
exercise: The magazine says magenta is «a pinky purple». Which colour is magenta? | Bright yellow | Pure black | A bright sky blue | *A bright purplish-red
exercise: Printed pictures are made of tiny dots of four inks. Which four are they? | *Cyan, magenta, yellow, black | Red, green, blue, white | Gold, silver, brown, pink | Cyan, magenta, yellow, white
test: In light, which two colours mix to make magenta? | Red and green | *Red and blue | Blue and yellow | Green and yellow
test: Where does the name magenta come from? | A printing company in London | A famous painter from Paris | *The town of Magenta in Italy | A lake in Scotland
exam: The magnifying glass shows «tiny dots of just four inks». How many inks make the picture? | Three | Five | Two | *Four
